{
  "brief_rationale": "The trajectory is closed after the doctor confirmed that the dressing was professionally opened and a 48-hour follow-up was set, without any self-initiated antibiotics. No serious responsibility-chain errors occurred. However, the doctor did not proactively ask or document systemic infection warning signs (fever/chills, pain worsening, expanding redness, purulent/odorous exudate, mental status change, SOB, nausea/vomiting) before closure, which is a minor omission for RC3. This caps the grade at borderline (2).",
